Z||000007||pontiacs4me||09-07-2001||02:26 PM||||first off you have to have a URL of the pic you want to post.  then type [img] before the URL including the <A HREF="http://......." TARGET=_blank>http://.......</A>   then type [/img] after the URL and up pops a pic.  this works with any bulletin board type system, its built into the internet.||||reg||1
Z||000008||MontanaFiero||09-07-2001||03:20 PM||||ahh-- a fellow mac fan!!! <BR> <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/ik72415.jpg"> <P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://members.home.net/blee291/fiero/mtfieroplate.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||beer_stud_21||09-07-2001||05:04 PM||||Hey all yee fellow fiero lovin mac users.  I was thinkin about trying to make a Mac version of pip but cliff never responded to my email about the info i would need to make a mac version.  Anyway.  For any of you who want to post pics from your mac heree is the best way.<P>#1) Sign up for a iTools account from apple.  You can do that <A HREF="http://www.apple.com/idisk" TARGET=_blank>here.</A><P>#2 Login to your iDisk.  You need to be running I believe OS 9 or above for this.   You login from the same url above.  <A HREF="http://www.apple.com/idisk/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.apple.com/idisk/</A> <P>#3 Upload your pictures into your "sites" folder.  <P>#4 Place " "[IMG]" then "http://homepage.mac.com/youritoolsname/yourpicturename" then "[/IMG] "  into your post here on PFF.  <P>Also note that once you have an itools account you will have a POP email account under that name.  iTools gives you 5mb worth of space.  This will be used up by your pictures you post, but you can also use the same space to host your own website.  The address will be the same as the URL to your pictures.  <P>If any of you try this and have trouble let me know.  My icq number is 8273989.  I would be happy to trade mac know how for fiero know how    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>-Marlin<p>[This message has been edited by beer_stud_21 (edited 09-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||pontiacs4me||09-07-2001||06:12 PM||||beer stud, <BR>I like my method, seems to be a bit easier.  only takes a second.  I used to just post links to my pics, and i never knew about adding the [img]....[/img] to make it seen.   Ill just stick with what I know.||||reg||1
Z||000011||beer_stud_21||09-07-2001||07:59 PM||||pontiacs3me,<P>I see that you have your own webspace to upload your pictures to.  I gave the instructions above mostly to give the other mac guys a way to post pictures here on PFF.  Because not everyone has their own webspace available.  With the method described above any mac user running a current version of the Mac OS can have have thier own website/email and use the space to store their fiero pictures.  So your probably better off doing things the way you have been, but for MinnGreenGT, or skitime they should try the method I described.  The iDisk works much better than those other sites like photopoint et all.<P>-Marlin||||reg||1
